# Project: agentic-airline-platform

## What This Project Is

An AI-native airline booking platform built entirely by AI agents. The real goal is to demonstrate a complete AI-driven SDLC: requirements → architecture → code → tests → deployment.

## Active Services (Version 1)

1. **flight-service** — Java 21 + Spring Boot 3 — manages flight data
2. **booking-service** — Java 21 + Spring Boot 3 — manages reservations
3. **payment-service** — NestJS (TypeScript) — handles payments
4. **ticket-service** — Java 21 + Spring Boot 3 — generates tickets and PNR

## Repository Structure

```
agentic-airline-platform/
├── .cursor/rules/          ← Cursor agent personas (this folder)
├── agents/                 ← LangGraph Python pipeline agents
├── docs/
│   ├── 01-vision/
│   ├── 02-requirements/
│   ├── 03-architecture/
│   ├── 04-prompts/
│   ├── 05-standards/       ← ai-rules.md, technology-stack.md
│   ├── 06-decisions/
│   └── templates/          ← module-template.md
├── modules/
│   └── {service-name}/
│       ├── docs/
│       │   ├── requirements.md
│       │   └── architecture.md
│       └── src/            ← generated source code lives here
└── infra/                  ← Docker, CI/CD configs
```

## Coding Standards

Always follow `docs/05-standards/ai-rules.md`:
- Clean Architecture: Controller → Service → Repository
- DTOs for all API payloads — never expose domain entities
- Global exception handler for all errors
- Bean Validation on all request DTOs
- OpenAPI annotations on all endpoints
- JUnit5 tests for Java, Jest for Node, pytest for Python

## Technology Stack

See `docs/05-standards/technology-stack.md` for the full list. Core:
- Java services: Java 21 + Spring Boot 3 + Maven
- Node services: NestJS + TypeScript
- Python agents: LangGraph + Ollama
- Messaging: Kafka
- Database: PostgreSQL (per service) + Redis

## Output Rules for All Agents

- Always save requirements to: `modules/{service-name}/docs/requirements.md`
- Always save architecture to: `modules/{service-name}/docs/architecture.md`
- Always save source code to: `modules/{service-name}/src/`
- Always save infra configs to: `infra/{service-name}/`
- Follow the module template at: `docs/templates/module-template.md`
